{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 27,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had bound him, they led ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away, and delivered him to Pontius Pilate the governor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Judas, who had betrayed him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented and brought again the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, I have sinned in that I have betrayed innocent blood. And they said, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to us? see thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he cast down the pieces of silver in the temple, and departed, and went and hanged himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the chief priests took the silver pieces, and said, It is not lawful to put them into the treasury, because it is the price of blood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they took counsel, and bought with them the potter's field, to bury strangers in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore that field has been called, The field of blood, to this day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremiah the prophet, saying, And they took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him that was valued, whom they of the children of Israel did value;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And gave them for the potter's field, as the Lord appointed me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And Jesus said to him, Thou sayest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he was accused by the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith Pilate to him, Hearest thou not how many things they testify against thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he answered him to not a word; so that the governor marveled greatly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now at ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feast, the governor was wont to release to the people a prisoner, whom they would.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they had then a notable prisoner, called Barabbas.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore when they were assembled, Pilate said to them, Whom will ye that I release to you? Barabbas, or Jesus, who is called Christ?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For he knew that for envy they had delivered him.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he was sitting on the judgment-seat, his wife sent to him, saying, Have thou nothing to do with that just man: for I have suffered many things this day in a dream, because of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas, and destroy Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The governor answered and said to them, Which of the two will ye that I release to you? They said, Barabbas.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pilate saith to them, What shall I do then with Jesus, who is called Christ? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "They",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all say to him, Let him be crucified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the governor said, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out the more, saying, Let him be crucified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Pilate saw that he could not prevail at all, but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rather a tumult was made, he took water, and washed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hands before the multitude, saying, I am innocent of the blood of this just person: see ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered all the people, and said, His blood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on us, and on our children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he released Barabbas to them: and when he had scourged Jesus, he delivered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be crucified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the common hall, and gathered to him the whole band ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of soldiers",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they stripped him, and put on him a scarlet robe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had platted a crown of thorns, they put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon his head, and a reed in his right hand: and they bowed the knee before him, and mocked him, saying, Hail, King of the Jews?",
          "kind": "text"
