      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then were there two thieves crucified with him: one on the right hand, and another on the left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that passed by, reviled him, wagging their heads,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And saying, Thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in three days, save thyself. If thou art the Son of God, come down from the cross.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise also the chief priests mocking ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", with the scribes and elders, said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He saved others; himself he cannot save. If he is King of Israel, let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He trusted in God; let him deliver him now if he will have him: for he said, I am the Son of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The thieves also who were crucified with him, cast the same in his teeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land to the ninth hour.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Some of them that stood there, when they heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " calleth for Elijah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And immediately one of them ran, and took a spunge, and filled ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with vinegar, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on a reed, and gave him to drink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rest said, Forbear, let us see whether Elijah will come to save him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus, when he had cried again with a loud voice, expired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, the vail of the temple was rent in two, from the top to the bottom: and the earth shook, and the rocks rent;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.27.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.27.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the graves were opened, and many bodies of saints who slept, arose,",
